    {"id": "CW-046", "language": "python", "description": "Bound concurrency with asyncio.Semaphore to N concurrent fetches", "implementation": "import asyncio, aiohttp\nasync def bounded_fetch(semaphore, session, url):\n    async with semaphore:\n        async with session.get(url) as r:\n            return await r.text()\n\nasync def fetch_all(urls, concurrency=5):\n    sem = asyncio.Semaphore(concurrency)\n    async with aiohttp.ClientSession() as session:\n        return await asyncio.gather(*(bounded_fetch(sem, session, u) for u in urls))", "explanation": "Semaphore caps simultaneous in-flight requests. Without it, gather() schedules all coroutines at once, which may overload the target (or your local socket pool). Concurrency 5 is a sensible starting default; tune to the target's rate limits. The session is shared so connections are reused."},
