    {"id": "CW-058", "language": "python", "description": "Format a duration in human-readable form (e.g. 1h 23m 45s)", "implementation": "def format_duration(seconds: int) -> str:\n    h, rem = divmod(seconds, 3600)\n    m, s = divmod(rem, 60)\n    parts = []\n    if h: parts.append(f'{h}h')\n    if m: parts.append(f'{m}m')\n    parts.append(f'{s}s')\n    return ' '.join(parts)", "explanation": "divmod(a, b) returns (a//b, a%b) in one call. Strips leading zero parts (60s -> '1m 0s' not '0h 1m 0s'). For locale-aware human time formatting use the humanize library: humanize.naturaldelta(timedelta)."},
