    {"id": "CW-059", "language": "python", "description": "Compute SHA-256 hash of a file in chunks (memory-efficient)", "implementation": "import hashlib\ndef sha256_file(path: str) -> str:\n    h = hashlib.sha256()\n    with open(path, 'rb') as f:\n        for chunk in iter(lambda: f.read(64 * 1024), b''):\n            h.update(chunk)\n    return h.hexdigest()", "explanation": "Reading in 64 KB chunks keeps memory bounded regardless of file size — important for multi-GB files. iter(callable, sentinel) calls the function until it returns the sentinel value (here empty bytes = EOF). hexdigest returns the hash as 64 hex chars; digest returns 32 raw bytes."},
    {"id": "CW-060", "language": "python", "description": "Base64-encode a binary blob with URL-safe alphabet", "implementation": "import base64\nencoded = base64.urlsafe_b64encode(blob).rstrip(b'=').decode()", "explanation": "Standard base64 uses + and / which are problematic in URLs. urlsafe_b64encode swaps them for - and _. Padding ('=') can be safely stripped (decode side accepts both). To decode, pad back to a multiple of 4 chars before calling urlsafe_b64decode. Useful for token IDs, JWT segments, file IDs in URLs."},
    {"id": "CW-061", "language": "python", "description": "HMAC-SHA256 a message with a secret key", "implementation": "import hmac, hashlib\ndef sign(message: bytes, key: bytes) -> str:\n    return hmac.new(key, message, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n\ndef verify(message: bytes, key: bytes, signature: str) -> bool:\n    expected = sign(message, key)\n    return hmac.compare_digest(expected, signature)", "explanation": "HMAC binds the hash to a secret, preventing forged messages. sha256 is the standard inner hash. CRITICAL: always use hmac.compare_digest for comparison; == is timing-attack vulnerable because it short-circuits on the first mismatch byte. compare_digest takes constant time regardless of where bytes differ."},
